WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.991
<v Examiner>Oestrogen, progesterone, and the pill.

2
00:00:03.991 --> 00:00:04.738
<v Examiner>Five marks.

3
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:09.348
<v Examiner>Describe the physiological effects of oestrogen and progesterone,

4
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:12.612
<v Examiner>including the female secondary sex characteristics,

5
00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.324
<v Examiner>and explain how the contraceptive pill prevents pregnancy.

6
00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:20.192
The hook: oestrogen builds, and progesterone prepares.

7
00:00:20.192 --> 00:00:24.433
The pill works three ways: no egg, a mucus plug, and a thin lining.

8
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:29.200
Oestrogen, from the granulosa cells of the follicle, rises at puberty.

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.579
It promotes oogenesis and follicle growth, and grows the uterine tubes,

10
00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:36.046
the uterus and the vagina to adult size.

11
00:00:36.046 --> 00:00:41.474
Its secondary sex characteristics: breast growth, fat laid down on the hips and breasts,

12
00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.743
a wider, lighter pelvis, and axillary and pubic hair.

13
00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:49.800
And in each cycle, oestrogen rebuilds the endometrium, in the proliferative phase.

14
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:55.599
Progesterone, from the corpus luteum, prepares the endometrium for implantation,

15
00:00:55.599 --> 00:00:57.137
in the secretory phase.

16
00:00:57.137 --> 00:01:01.215
And in pregnancy, it develops the breast lobules and alveoli.

17
00:01:02.665 --> 00:01:08.676
The pill contains synthetic oestrogen and progestin, which is a synthetic progesterone,

18
00:01:08.676 --> 00:01:11.163
either combined, or progestin alone.

19
00:01:11.163 --> 00:01:13.443
It prevents pregnancy three ways.

20
00:01:13.443 --> 00:01:14.756
It stops ovulation.

21
00:01:14.756 --> 00:01:19.385
It thickens the cervical mucus, so sperm can't get into the uterus.

22
00:01:19.385 --> 00:01:23.807
And it thins the endometrium, so a fertilised egg can't implant.

23
00:01:25.257 --> 00:01:25.946
The traps.

24
00:01:25.946 --> 00:01:30.567
Oestrogen: the ducts, the fat, the pelvis, the proliferative phase.

25
00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:34.566
Progesterone: the alveoli, the secretory phase, pregnancy.

26
00:01:34.566 --> 00:01:39.256
Second: the pill works three ways, so name all three for full marks.

27
00:01:39.256 --> 00:01:43.049
Third: progestin is the synthetic form of progesterone.

28
00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:44.121
<v Examiner>Once more.

29
00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:46.485
<v Examiner>Oestrogen, progesterone, and the pill.

30
00:01:48.935 --> 00:01:52.232
Oestrogen rises at puberty and drives follicle growth.

31
00:01:52.232 --> 00:01:56.566
It grows the uterine tubes, uterus and vagina; it brings breast growth,

32
00:01:56.566 --> 00:02:01.572
fat on the hips and breasts, a wider, lighter pelvis, and axillary and pubic hair;

33
00:02:01.572 --> 00:02:05.174
and it rebuilds the endometrium in the proliferative phase.

34
00:02:05.174 --> 00:02:09.692
Progesterone, from the corpus luteum, readies the lining for implantation,

35
00:02:09.692 --> 00:02:12.744
and in pregnancy develops the lobules and alveoli.

36
00:02:12.744 --> 00:02:18.239
The pill, synthetic oestrogen and progestin, stops ovulation, thickens the cervical mucus,

37
00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:19.826
and thins the endometrium.
